[!] Enable:
[!] -electrumwallet FILE1 FILE2 ... Load Electrum wallet files.
[!] -electrumwallet -f DIR          Recursively scan .wallet/.dat/.json/no-extension files.
[!]                                 Text/hash files with $electrum$5 and $electrum$2 lines are imported too.

[!] Candidate sources:
[!] -i FILE                        Dictionary/password list, repeatable.
[!] -hex                           Dictionary lines are hex-encoded password bytes.
[!] -mask MASK                     GPU mask brute force.
[!] -mask-file FILE                One mask per line.
[!] -start HEX [-end HEX]          Raw byte range, length-major, up to 127 bytes.
[!] -n N                           Optional generated-candidate launch window.

[!] Save format:
[!] ELECTRUMWALLET:<file>:PASSWORD:<password>:TYPE:<BIE1|FIELD|PLAINTEXT>:DETAIL:<hash>

[!] Example:
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -electrumwallet -f electrum_wallets -i passwords.txt -save

[!] ======================================================================
[!] MAIN MODE: -walletscan  (host-only wallet artifact inventory)
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Purpose:
[!] Fast read-only inventory for text-like wallet artifacts.
[!] Validates and extracts WIF/xprv/xpub through Base58Check, mnemonic candidates through embedded BIP39 wordlists,
[!] SECO indicators, Armory binary wallets/plaintext Armory root+priv records, and protobuf-like .wallet files.
[!] Does not brute-force passwords.
[!] Findings are printed to console unless -silent is used; -save/-o also writes them to file.

[!] Enable:
[!] -walletscan FILE1 FILE2 ...    Scan explicit files.
[!] -walletscan -f DIR             Recursively scan .txt/.json/.dat/.wallet/.ldb/.log/.seco/no-extension files.

[!] ======================================================================
[!] MAIN MODE: -walletjs  (JS/browser wallet research profiles)
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Purpose:
[!] JS/browser wallet research pipelines on GPU.
[!] Enabled profiles are kept explicit and reference-vector gated.

[!] Enable:
[!] -walletjs cryptojs-sha256      SHA256(password bytes) brainwallet style.
[!] -walletjs bitaddress-sha256    Alias for SHA256(password bytes).
[!] -walletjs jsbn-arc4-v8-2011    JSBN ARC4 V8 2011 bounded seed profile.
[!] -walletjs jsbn-arc4-v8-2015    JSBN ARC4 V8 2015 bounded seed profile.
[!] -walletjs jsbn-arc4-spidermonkey-lcg48
[!] -walletjs jsbn-arc4-jsc-weakrandom
[!] -walletjs jsbn-arc4-v8-2011-exact
[!] -walletjs jsbn-arc4-v8-2015-exact
[!] -walletjs jsbn-arc4-spidermonkey-lcg48-exact
[!] -walletjs jsbn-arc4-jsc-weakrandom-exact

[!] Candidate sources:
[!] SHA256/password profiles:
[!] -i FILE                         Dictionary/password list.
[!] -hex                            Dictionary lines are hex-encoded bytes.
[!] -mask MASK                      GPU mask brute force, example: "?l?l?l?d?d".
[!] -mask-file FILE                 One mask per line.
[!] -start HEX                      First raw-byte password candidate.
[!] -end HEX                        Last raw-byte password candidate.
[!]
[!] Browser seed profiles:
[!] -s HEX                          Start seed.
[!] -e HEX                          End seed.
[!] -random                         Randomize seed windows inside -s/-e.
[!] -n N                            Launch/check window size.
[!] Large GPU filters lower auto occupancy where needed to avoid VRAM/cache pressure.
[!]
[!] Exact JSBN ARC4 profiles:
[!] -s HEX                          Start Math.random state seed.
[!] -e HEX                          End Math.random state seed.
[!] -time-s HEX                     Start low32 Date.getTime() seed.
[!] -time-e HEX                     End low32 Date.getTime() seed.
[!] -time-delta N                   Check second rng_seed_time as time0 + 0..N ms, default 0.

[!] Save format:
[!] WALLETJS:<profile>:SOURCE:<password>:PRIV:<private64hex>:<TYPE>:<payload>
[!] WALLETJS:<profile>:SOURCE:<seed64hex>:PRIV:<private64hex>:<TYPE>:<payload>
[!] WALLETJS:<profile>:SOURCE:state=<seed64>;t0=<time32>;t1=<time32>:PRIV:<private64hex>:<TYPE>:<payload>

[!] Examples:
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -walletjs cryptojs-sha256 -i passwords.txt -c e -hash <eth20>
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -walletjs jsbn-arc4-v8-2011 -s 0 -e ffffffff -c e -xc targets.xor
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -walletjs jsbn-arc4-v8-2011-exact -s 0 -e ffffffff -time-s 5a000000 -time-e 5a00ffff -time-delta 2 -c cus -xu BTC_0.xor_u

[!] ======================================================================
[!] MAIN MODE: -mnemonic (DEFAULT BASIC MODE)
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Purpose:
[!] Basic mnemonic mode. If no other main mode selected, this mode runs.

[!] Enable:
[!] -mnemonic                      default mode

[!] Submodes:
[!] -mnemonic 1                    sha256 (1 iter in basic).
[!] -mnemonic 2                    sha512 (1 iter in basic).
[!] -mnemonic 3                    keccak256 (1 iter in basic).
[!] -mnemonic 4                    sha3-256 (1 iter in basic).
[!] -mnemonic 5                    md5 (1 iter in basic).
[!] -mnemonic 6                    hexing function.
[!] -mnemonic -scramble [WORDS]    Unique multiset permutations on Metal.
[!]
[!] Scramble input / positional restrictions:
[!] -scramble "WORDS"              Inline 12/15/18/21/24-word BIP39 phrase.
[!] -i FILE                        One scramble phrase per line; repeatable.
[!] -pattern "TOKENS"              One token per output position:
[!]                                * = any remaining phrase word;
[!]                                word = fix that word at this position;
[!]                                {word|word} = restrict this position.
[!] -pattern-file FILE             Read exactly one non-comment pattern.
[!] -start N / -end N              Checked U256 permutation ordinal range;
[!]                                end is exclusive and defaults to the full
[!]                                unique-multiset permutation domain.
[!] -n N                           Completed permutation ordinals per batch.
[!] -wallet-mem auto|all|NN%|SIZE  Unified-memory budget; MiB/GiB supported.
[!] Duplicate words are handled as a multiset, so identical permutations are
[!] not repeated. Metal unrank/checksum runs first; only checksum-valid BIP39
[!] phrases enter seed, derivation and exact target verification. Overflow
[!] halves and repeats the uncredited window. MultiGPU intervals do not overlap.
[!] SpeedThreadFunc is the only live statistics printer (Candidate/s).
[!] Examples:
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -mnemonic -scramble \
[!]   "abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon abandon about" \
[!]   -pattern "* * * * * * * * * * * *" -d paths.txt -c c -hash HEX
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -mnemonic -scramble -i phrases.txt \
[!]   -pattern-file positions.txt -start 0 -end 0x100000 \
[!]   -wallet-mem all -device 0 -d paths.txt -c p -hash HEX

[!] Required / input:
[!] -d FILE                        BIP derivation paths file for address/path checks.
[!]                                DOT can use -d-dot without -d.
[!] -i FILE                        Input file with mnemonic/text candidates. STDIN is used when -i is not set.
[!] -hex                           Parse input lines as hex bytes before mnemonic/hash flow.
[!]
[!] Mnemonic/hash flow:
[!] -iter LIST                     Hash rounds list for selected -mnemonic submode.
[!] -utf8                          Re-hash using UTF-8 hex text between iterations.
[!] -text                          Store hash output as text payload.
[!] -pass FILE                     BIP39 passphrase list file.
[!] -passbrute                     Brute-force BIP39 passphrase branch.
[!] -dub                           Duplicate/passphrase helper used by BIP39 flows.
[!] -electrum [seg]                Electrum v2 style mnemonic; optional seg variant.
[!] -128                           Electrum 128-bit style toggle.
[!] -ton / -TON                    TON mnemonic style toggle.
[!] -pbkdf N                       PBKDF rounds override.
[!] -round N                       Plus/minus rounds around each derived private key.
[!]
[!] Thread-split / invert modes:
[!] -pass_thread                   One mnemonic input per round; passphrase candidates
[!]                                from -pass/-passbrute are split across GPU threads/GPUs.
[!]                                This is for explicit input/file/STDIN flows, not PRNG,
[!]                                seq/random, hexset, or recovery branches.
[!] -der_thread                    One mnemonic/passphrase source per round; derivation
[!]                                paths from -d/-d-type/-d-dot are split across GPU threads/GPUs.
[!]                                Also supported with -mnemonic -prng/-prng64 generation.
[!]                                Do not combine with -pass_thread, -hexset, or recovery.
[!]
[!] Sequential mode:
[!] -start HEX                     First generated payload point for seq branch.
[!] -end HEX                       Last generated payload point for seq branch.
[!] -step HEX                      Step between seq points, default 1.
[!] -back                          Walk backward from -start.
[!] -both                          Without -end: walk both directions around -start.
[!]                                With -start/-end: + starts at -start, - starts at -end.
[!] -random                        Without -start: standalone random branch; with -start/-end: seq-random.
[!] -n N                           Random/check window size for seq-random branch.
[!]
[!] PRNG mode:
[!] -prng                          Use internal 32-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -prng64                        Use internal 64-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -gen LIST                      Generator IDs list/range.
[!] -mode LIST                     Byte extraction mode IDs list/range.
[!] -byte LIST                     Generated byte sizes list/range.
[!] -shift LIST                    Skip counts list/range.
[!] -s HEX                         PRNG start seed.
[!] -e HEX                         PRNG end seed.
[!] -random                        Randomize PRNG seed selection.
[!]
[!] Hexset sequential mode:
[!] -hexset HEXDIGITS              Hex alphabet, 1..16 unique nibbles in user order.
[!] -start HEX                     Required even-length hex lower bound.
[!] -end HEX                       Optional even-length hex upper bound.
[!]
[!] Hexset recovery mode:
[!] -recovery TEMPLATE             Inline hex template; * means one unknown hex nibble.
[!] -recovery -i FILE              Template file, one template per line.
[!] -hexset HEXDIGITS              Alphabet used to fill * positions.
[!]
[!] Example:
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -mnemonic -pass pass.txt -d derivations.txt -i in.txt -c cuspex -bf bloom.blf

