[!] -gen LIST                      Generator IDs list/range.
[!] -mode LIST                     Byte extraction mode IDs list/range.
[!] -byte LIST                     Generated byte sizes list/range.
[!] -shift LIST                    Skip counts list/range.
[!] -s HEX                         PRNG start seed.
[!] -e HEX                         PRNG end seed.
[!] -random                        Randomize PRNG seed selection.
[!]
[!] Hexset sequential mode:
[!] -hexset HEXDIGITS              Hex alphabet, 1..16 unique nibbles in user order.
[!] -start HEX                     Required even-length hex lower bound.
[!] -end HEX                       Optional even-length hex upper bound.
[!]
[!] Hexset recovery mode:
[!] -recovery TEMPLATE             Inline hex template; * means one unknown hex nibble.
[!] -recovery -i FILE              Template file, one template per line.
[!] -hexset HEXDIGITS              Alphabet used to fill * positions.
[!]
[!] Example:
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -entropy 1 -sizes 16,20,24,32 -lang EN -d derivations.txt -i entropy.txt -c cuspex

[!] ======================================================================
[!] MAIN MODE: -bip32
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Purpose:
[!] Treat input as BIP32 passphrase payload (pre-seed stage).

[!] Enable:
[!] -bip32                         default HMAC-SHA256 mode from bip32.org (50000 iters in basic).

[!] Submodes:
[!] -bip32 1                       sha256.
[!] -bip32 2                       sha512.
[!] -bip32 3                       keccak256.
[!] -bip32 4                       sha3-256.
[!] -bip32 5                       md5.
[!] -bip32 6                       passthrough (no hash pre-stage).

[!] Required / input:
[!] -d FILE                        BIP derivation paths file for address/path checks.
[!]                                DOT can use -d-dot without -d.
[!] -i FILE                        BIP32 passphrase payload file. STDIN is used when -i is not set.
[!] -hex                           Input lines are hex-encoded bytes.
[!] -iter LIST                     Iterations list for selected -bip32 submode.
[!] -utf8                          UTF-8 text flow between iterations.
[!] -round N                       Plus/minus rounds around each generated key.
[!]
[!] Derivation-thread mode:
[!] -der_thread                    One BIP32 payload line per round; derivation paths
[!]                                from -d/-d-type/-d-dot are split across GPU threads/GPUs.
[!]                                This is for explicit input/file/STDIN flows only.
[!]                                Do not combine with -prng/-prng64, seq/random, hexset,
[!]                                mode-scoped recovery, or -pass_thread.
[!]
[!] Sequential mode:
[!] -start HEX                     First byte/payload point for seq branch.
[!] -end HEX                       Last byte/payload point for seq branch.
[!] -step HEX                      Step between seq points, default 1.
[!] -back                          Walk backward from -start.
[!] -both                          Without -end: walk both directions around -start.
[!]                                With -start/-end: + starts at -start, - starts at -end.
[!] -random                        With -start/-end, choose random points inside that range.
[!] -n N                           Seq-random span/check window.
[!]
[!] PRNG mode:
[!] -prng                          Use internal 32-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -prng64                        Use internal 64-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -gen LIST                      Generator IDs list/range.
[!] -mode LIST                     Byte extraction mode IDs list/range.
[!] -byte LIST                     Generated byte sizes list/range.
[!] -shift LIST                    Skip counts list/range.
[!] -s HEX                         PRNG start seed.
[!] -e HEX                         PRNG end seed.
[!] -random                        Randomize PRNG seed selection.
[!]
[!] Hexset sequential mode:
[!] -hexset HEXDIGITS              Hex alphabet, 1..16 unique nibbles in user order.
[!] -start HEX                     Required even-length hex lower bound.
[!] -end HEX                       Optional even-length hex upper bound.
[!]
[!] Hexset recovery mode:
[!] -recovery TEMPLATE             Inline hex template; * means one unknown hex nibble.
[!] -recovery -i FILE              Template file, one template per line.
[!] -hexset HEXDIGITS              Alphabet used to fill * positions.
[!]
[!] Example:
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -bip32 2 -iter 1-5 -hex -d derivations.txt -i passphrases.txt -c cuspex

