[!] randstorm, randstorm:jsbn        Source-grounded BitcoinJS SecureRandom scan:
[!]                                  JSBN BigInteger(256,rng), double seedTime,
[!]                                  high/low and low/high pool-order variants.
[!]                                  Legacy brand synonyms remain parser-only.
[!] randstorm:all                    JSBN plus explicit raw/pool compatibility variants.
[!] randstorm:core-jsbn              Narrow 4-engine JSBN reference set.
[!] randstorm:raw32                  Compatibility with raw ARC4/pool32 bytes.
[!] randstorm:pool32                 SecureRandom2-style raw first-32 pool bytes.
[!] randstorm-bytes                  BitcoinJS Crypto.util.randomBytes(32):
[!]                                  byte = floor(Math.random()*256), no JSBN/ARC4.
[!]                                  Add :low8 for low-byte lane variants.
[!]                                  Service/random-button names fold into this
[!]                                  one alias; duplicate brand aliases rejected.
[!] coinpunk-browserify-jsbn         Coinpunk browserify SecureRandom path:
[!]                                  crypto-browserify randomBytes(1) per JSBN byte,
[!]                                  BigInteger(256,rng) 33-byte draw then mod(n-1)+1.
[!]                                  Legacy browserify synonyms remain parser-only.
[!] randstorm-pymt                   RandstormBTC Python PoC model:
[!]                                  random.seed(seed), randint(0,255) x32.
[!]                                  Legacy RandstormBTC synonyms remain parser-only.
[!] phpcoinaddress                   PHPCoinAddress mt_rand raw private key profile.
[!]                                  Variants: php521 = MT_RAND_PHP,
[!]                                  php710 = MT_RAND_MT19937,
[!]                                  phplegacy = PHP 3.0.7-5.2.0 mt_rand.
[!]                                  Default all.
[!]                                  Uses -s/-e as 32-bit mt_srand seed range and
[!]                                  -n as sequential generated keys/offsets per seed.
[!]                                  Covers Milk Sad #17/#18 PHPCoinAddress
[!]                                  BTC/BCH/LTC-style direct secp key usage.
[!] elliptic-php-rand-hmacdrbg      simplito/elliptic-php PHP 5 fallback:
[!]                                  if random_int() is missing, Utils.php defines
[!]                                  random_int($a,$b) as rand($a,$b). EC::genKeyPair()
[!]                                  fills 192 rand(0,255) entropy bytes, appends
[!]                                  the secp256k1 order as HMAC-DRBG nonce, then
[!]                                  accepts HMAC-SHA256 output <= n-2 and adds 1.
[!]                                  One alias covers concrete PHP rand runtimes:
[!]                                  php5-random, php5-lrand48, php5-rand15,
[!]                                  php5-zts-rand-r31, php5-zts-rand-r15.
[!]                                  Uses -s/-e as 32-bit PHP rand seed range and
[!]                                  -n as sequential genKeyPair() calls per seed.
[!] bluewallet-isaac                 BlueWallet v0.9.7/v2.x/v3.0 isaac@0.0.5
[!]                                  family. One alias covers direct-private
[!]                                  cap255/cap256 byte-scale variants and
[!]                                  the v3.0.0 HD/BIP39 subprofile.
[!]                                  Uses -s/-e as effective 32-bit module-load
[!]                                  ISAAC seed. Direct variants use -n as
[!]                                  sequential wallets; hd-v3 emits one
[!]                                  BIP39 mnemonic per seed and defaults to
[!]                                  m/49'/0'/0'/0/0 when -d is not supplied.
[!] time-lcg-direct                  B4Q/source-derived direct private-key LCG
[!]                                  byte lanes. One alias covers glibc, MSVC,
[!]                                  Borland Delphi, dual glibc/MSVC XOR, and
[!]                                  explicit glibc-xor-pid time^PID seeding.
[!]                                  Uses -s/-e as effective 32-bit seed and
[!]                                  -n as sequential generated keys/offsets.
[!]                                  For glibc-xor-pid, -s/-e are Unix-time
[!]                                  seconds and PID is swept 1..32768.
[!] time-mt                         B4Q/source-described MT19937 timestamp
[!]                                  direct private-key profile. One alias for
[!]                                  standard MT19937 seeded by 32-bit Unix
[!]                                  timestamp/effective seed, then 8 tempered
[!]                                  u32 values used as little-endian U256 limbs.
[!]                                  Uses -s/-e as 32-bit seed range and -n as
[!]                                  sequential generated keys from that MT stream.
[!] java-lcg-direct                  B4Q/source-derived Java Random.nextBytes(32)
[!]                                  direct private-key profile. One alias for
[!]                                  java.util.Random 48-bit LCG nextBytes,
[!]                                  seeded by bounded constructor/effective seed.
[!]                                  Uses -s/-e as effective 48-bit seed and
[!]                                  -n as sequential generated keys/offsets.
[!] tezosj-java-random               TezosJ_plainJava mnemonic entropy profile:
[!]                                  java.util.Random().nextBytes(20) then
[!]                                  BIP39 MnemonicCode.toMnemonic(bytes).
[!]                                  Uses explicit bounded -s/-e over 48-bit
[!]                                  Java constructor seeds; emits one mnemonic
[!]                                  per seed. No default derivation path is
[!]                                  added because TezosJ source uses first
[!]                                  32 bytes of BIP39 seed for libsodium keys.
[!] sha256-direct                    B4Q/source-derived SHA256 direct private-key
[!]                                  profile. One alias covers decimal number
[!]                                  strings, 16-char zero-padded lowercase hex,
[!]                                  10-digit zero-padded phone strings,
[!]                                  printable ASCII strings length 1-6, and
[!]                                  B4Q be64 / be64d binary-counter modes.
[!]                                  Uses -s/-e as numeric input range; -n must be 1.
[!] pid-hash-direct                 B4Q mode 10 simplified CVE-2008-0166 PID
[!]                                  hash candidate: private_key =
[!]                                  SHA256(SHA256(pid_as_4_bytes_big_endian)).
[!]                                  Uses -s/-e as PID range 0..ffff; -n must be 1.
[!] lowbits-direct                  B4Q mode 6 low/private-key counter profile:
[!]                                  private key = 32-byte big-endian counter
[!]                                  (key = 1, 2, 3, ...). Uses -s/-e as
[!]                                  uint64 counter range; -n must be 1.
[!] pybtc-mt                        vbuterin/pybitcointools random_key() /
[!]                                  random_electrum_seed(): Python MT19937,
[!]                                  private key = SHA256(random_string(32) +
[!]                                  str(random.randrange(2^256)) + str(ts)).
[!]                                  Two variants via -v: random-key (default
[!]                                  both) and electrum-seed. Two time modes
[!]                                  selected by the sub-alias suffix:
[!]                                  pybtc-mt:nots sweeps only the 32-bit
[!]                                  MT19937 seed (-s/-e), timestamp omitted;
[!]                                  pybtc-mt:ts additionally sweeps a known
[!]                                  microsecond timestamp low32 window via
[!]                                  -time-s/-time-e (reinterpreted as
[!]                                  microseconds, not JS ms). -s/-e are the
[!]                                  MT19937 seed32 range; -n = sequential
[!]                                  keys per seed.
[!] nano-java-random                 Nano (RaiBlocks) Android generateSeed():
[!]                                  java.util.Random 48-bit LCG, build a
[!]                                  64-char hex seed by concatenating
[!]                                  Integer.toHexString(nextInt()) x16, then
[!]                                  SHA-256 the ASCII hex string. -s/-e are
[!]                                  the 48-bit Java Random constructor seed
[!]                                  range; -n = sequential seeds. NOTE: no
[!]                                  Nano/Ed25519 address derivation is present
[!]                                  here, so the 32-byte seed is emitted as a
[!]                                  secp256k1 key-material candidate matched
[!]                                  against c/u/s/p/r/x/e filters.
[!] pywallet-ts-weak                ranaroussi/pywallet new_random_wallet():
[!]                                  seed = str(urandom(64)) + str(int(
[!]                                  time.time()*1e6)). Brute-forceable only
[!]                                  under the compromised-urandom assumption
[!]                                  with a known timestamp window. -s/-e are
[!]                                  the microsecond timestamp range; -n must
[!]                                  be 1. Emits SHA256(b'\x00' repr + ts) as
[!]                                  a secp256k1 key-material candidate (the
[!]                                  full BIP32/BIP39 wallet tree is not modeled).
[!] B4Q duplicate-name coverage     No duplicate aliases are added for mode names
[!]                                  that are already covered by one canonical
[!]                                  logic:
[!]                                  time-lcg-glibc -> time-lcg-direct:glibc
[!]                                  time-lcg-msvc -> time-lcg-direct:msvc
[!]                                  time-lcg-pid -> time-lcg-direct:glibc-xor-pid
[!]                                  borland-lcg -> time-lcg-direct:borland
[!]                                  lcg-usec-seed -> time-lcg-direct:glibc
[!]                                  dual-lcg-xor -> time-lcg-direct:dual-xor
[!]                                  sha256-time/ms-time -> sha256-direct:decimal
[!]                                  sha256-seq/sha256d-seq -> sha256-direct be64/be64d
[!]                                  sha256-decimal/hex/phone/short-ascii map to
[!]                                  sha256-direct variants.
[!]                                  Recognized but not implemented without
[!]                                  source-closed byte/private-key layout:
[!]                                  php-mt-seed, v8-xorshift128, openssl-debian.
