[!]
[!] Flags for -xp:
[!] -s HEX / -e HEX                  PID range for OpenSSL profiles. Default 0..8000.
[!]                                  Randstorm: required Math.random state/seed range.
[!]                                  randstorm-v8init: required C rand/random seed range.
[!]                                  phpcoinaddress: required PHP mt_srand seed range.
[!]                                  elliptic-php-rand-hmacdrbg: required PHP rand seed range.
[!]                                  bluewallet-isaac: required effective ISAAC seed.
[!]                                  time-lcg-direct: required effective 32-bit seed
[!]                                  or timestamp range for glibc-xor-pid.
[!]                                  time-mt: required 32-bit Unix timestamp/
[!]                                  effective seed range.
[!]                                  java-lcg-direct: required effective 48-bit seed.
[!]                                  tezosj-java-random: required bounded
[!]                                  48-bit Java constructor seed range.
[!]                                  sha256-direct: required numeric input range.
[!]                                  pid-hash-direct: required PID range 0..ffff.
[!]                                  lowbits-direct: required uint64 counter range.
[!] -n N                             OpenSSL: keys per PID. Randstorm: sequential
[!]                                  keys from one JSBN/SecureRandom/PHP mt_rand state.
[!]                                  time-mt/time-lcg/java-lcg direct modes:
[!]                                  sequential generated keys from one PRNG seed.
[!]                                  pybtc-mt/nano-java-random direct modes also
[!]                                  use -n as sequential keys from one PRNG seed.
[!]                                  sha256-direct/pid-hash-direct/lowbits-direct
[!]                                  require -n 1.
[!]                                  Default 1.
[!] -once                            One complete domain pass then exit for openssl:*.
[!]                                  Source/input profiles are one-pass by default.
[!] -i FILE                          Required for cgr-state/cgr-bridge/cgr-xor/cgr-chain/
[!]                                  cgr-chain-bridge/ssleay-stir input.
[!]                                  cgr-state/cgr-bridge/cgr-xor/cgr-chain/
[!]                                  cgr-chain-bridge/ssleay-stir/raw32 accept -i FILE
[!]                                  and/or -f DIR.
[!] -f DIR                           cgr-* source scan: recursively scan trace
[!]                                  artifacts for state20/aux20/raw20/prefix20.
[!]                                  raw32: recursively scan .json/.jsonl/
[!]                                  .txt/.log/.tsv artifacts and output-like .bin
[!]                                  files for output32 markers.
[!]                                  ssleay-stir: recursively load
[!]                                  ssleay_stir_randbytes_trace.jsonl files.
[!] -v VALUE                         Optional OpenSSL path restriction, same names as profiles.
[!]                                  Randstorm: optional engine/variant restriction.
[!]                                  v8-2011/v8-2015/spidermonkey-lcg48/jsc-weakrandom/
[!]                                  v8-classic-mwc/v8-alt-mwc/v8-mwc1616,
[!]                                  jsbn/jsbn-hilo/jsbn-lohi, raw32/raw32-hilo/
[!]                                  raw32-lohi, pool32/pool32-hilo/pool32-lohi,
[!]                                  jsbn-arc4-v8-2011, raw32-v8-2011,
[!]                                  pool32-v8-2011.
[!]                                  randstorm-v8init also accepts msvc/ansi/lrand48/glibc
[!]                                  with v8-2011/v8-2015/v8-alt-mwc/v8-mwc1616.
[!]                                  phpcoinaddress accepts all/php521/php710/phplegacy.
[!]                                  elliptic-php-rand-hmacdrbg accepts
[!]                                  all/php5-random/php5-lrand48/php5-rand15/
[!]                                  php5-zts-rand-r31/php5-zts-rand-r15.
[!]                                  bluewallet-isaac accepts all/v0-cap255/v2-cap256;
[!]                                  use -xp bluewallet-isaac:hd-v3 for HD/BIP39.
[!]                                  tezosj-java-random does not use -v; use -d
[!]                                  for derivation paths on supported targets.
[!]                                  time-lcg-direct accepts all/glibc/msvc/
[!]                                  borland/dual-xor/glibc-xor-pid.
[!]                                  time-mt does not use -v.
[!]                                  java-lcg-direct accepts all/nextbytes.
[!]                                  sha256-direct accepts all/decimal/hex/
[!]                                  phone10/short-ascii/be64/be64d.
[!]                                  pid-hash-direct accepts all/sha256d-pid-be4.
[!]                                  lowbits-direct accepts all/be64.
[!]                                  pybtc-mt accepts all/random-key/
[!]                                  electrum-seed; the time mode is set by the
[!]                                  pybtc-mt:ts / pybtc-mt:nots sub-alias suffix.
[!]                                  nano-java-random does not use -v.
[!]                                  pywallet-ts-weak does not use -v.
[!] -time-s HEX / -time-e HEX        Randstorm low32 Date.getTime() / seedTime range.
[!]                                  If omitted, time follows low32(state).
[!] -time-delta N                    Randstorm second seedTime delta in ms, default 0.
[!] -time-events N                   Extra JSBN rng_seed_time calls before ARC4, default 0.
[!] -time-events-repeat N            Extra JSBN rng_seed_time calls with same timestamp.
[!] -screen-seed X:Y                 Mix exact screenX/screenY seedInt values.
[!] -screen-seed-zero                Alias for -screen-seed 0:0.
[!] -time-mode state|seed-sec-ms|seed-ms-offset
[!]                                  Randstorm implicit time: source low32, seed*1000+offset,
[!]                                  or seed/source + millisecond offset.
[!] -mileage N                       Randstorm pre-consumed Math.random calls 0..N.
[!] -mileage-s N / -mileage-e N      Randstorm explicit pre-consumed Math.random range.
[!] -c TYPES                         Choose target families to verify.
[!]                                  Multiple letters allowed, example: -c cusrpex
[!]
)HELP" METAL_HELP_FULL_TARGET_TYPES_FOR_C R"HELP([!]
[!] With -c, at least one target type must be selected. Multiple types are allowed.
[!]
[!] -hash HEX                        Fast prefix/target payload match (2..32 bytes).
[!] -target HEX                      Alias for -hash in this mode.
[!] -bf PATH                         Bloom filter(s).
[!] -xu PATH                         XOR uncompressed filter(s).
[!] -xc PATH                         XOR compressed filter(s).
[!] -xuc PATH                        XOR ultra-compressed filter(s).
[!] -xh PATH                         XOR HC filter(s).
[!] -xx PATH                         Optional async CPU XOR false-positive postcheck.
[!] -xb PATH                         Optional async CPU Bloom false-positive postcheck.
[!] -save                            Save confirmed results.
[!] -o FILE                          Output file, default result.txt.
[!] -silent                          Do not print founds to console.
[!]
[!] Safe smoke-gate examples (aggregate counters only, no result save):
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -xp bluewallet-isaac:v2-cap256 -s 0 -e ffff -n 1 -c e -xc filters/EVM.xor_c -xx filters/EVM-1.xor_u -xx filters/EVM-2.xor_u -silent
