[!] ======================================================================
[!] MAIN MODE: -minikeys
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Purpose:
[!] Brute Casascius mini private keys directly on GPU (generation + validation on card).
[!]
[!] Enable:
[!] -minikeys
[!]
[!] Key types:
[!] 22 chars (S + 21 base58), 26 chars (S + 25), 30 chars (S + 29)
[!]
[!] Base mode flags:
[!] -round N                        Rounds applied after validated minikey private key.
[!]
[!] Sequential minikey mode:
[!] -start VALUE                    First minikey. Full S... key or suffix-only form is accepted.
[!] -end VALUE                      Last minikey. Must use the same full/suffix style as -start.
[!] -random                         Choose random minikey starts inside the selected range.
[!] -n N                            Random chunk/window size hint.
[!]
[!] SUFFIX USAGE (IMPORTANT):
[!] You can pass -start/-end in two formats:
[!] 1) Full mini key: starts with S (or s), total length 22/26/30.
[!] 2) Suffix only: without S, length 21/25/29.
[!]
[!] Length mapping:
[!] 22 (full) <-> 21 (suffix)
[!] 26 (full) <-> 25 (suffix)
[!] 30 (full) <-> 29 (suffix)
[!]
[!] Allowed symbols: Base58 only
[!] 123456789ABCDEFGHJKLMNPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijkmnopqrstuvwxyz
[!] (symbols 0, O, I, l are not allowed)
[!]
[!] Range behavior:
[!] -start only  -> end is auto-set to max suffix of the same type.
[!] -end only    -> start is auto-set to min suffix of the same type.
[!] -start + -end:
[!]    same type  -> requires start <= end.
[!]    different type -> scans all mini key types between start and end type.
[!]
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Submode: -minikeys -seed
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Purpose:
[!] Input is seed bytes/text. For each seed, GPU reproduces Casascius-style deterministic mini-key generation,
[!] then checks found private keys via standard mini-key pipeline.
[!]
[!] Flags for -minikeys -seed:
[!] -size N                         One final minikey length. Allowed: 22,26,30.
[!] -sizes LIST                     Multiple final minikey lengths. Default: all 22,26,30.
[!] -hex                            ON: input lines are HEX bytes, OFF: raw/text.
[!]
[!] Sequential seed mode:
[!] -start HEX                      First seed-byte point, up to 128 hex chars = 64 bytes.
[!] -end HEX                        Last seed-byte point, up to 128 hex chars = 64 bytes.
[!] -random                         Full random without -start, or seq-random inside -start/-end.
[!] -n N                            Random chunk size hint, counted as seed keys per random start.
[!]
[!] PRNG mode:
[!] -prng                           Use internal 32-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -prng64                         Use internal 64-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -gen LIST                       Generator IDs list/range.
[!] -mode LIST                      Byte extraction mode IDs list/range.
[!] -byte LIST                      Generated byte sizes list/range.
[!] -shift LIST                     Skip counts list/range.
[!] -s HEX                          PRNG start seed.
[!] -e HEX                          PRNG end seed.
[!]
[!] -round N                        Rounds are applied after generated mini private key.
[!]
[!] Notes:
[!] 1) Plain -minikeys (without -seed) does NOT use -prng/-prng64/-hex.
[!] 2) -minikeys -seed supports -prng/-prng64/-hex and seed-style -start/-end.
[!] 3) -d derivations is not used in both mini key modes.
[!]
[!] Examples:
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -minikeys -c cuspex -bf bloom.blf
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -minikeys -i minikeys.txt -c c
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -minikeys -start S111111111111111111111 -end Szzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzzz -random -n 2000000 -c c
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -minikeys -start 111111111111111111111 -end 11111111111111111111z -c c
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -minikeys -start 1111111111111111111111111 -end 111111111111111111111111z -c c
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -minikeys -seed -hex -i seeds_hex.txt -sizes 22,30 -c c
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -minikeys -seed -start 1 -end FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF -size 26 -c c
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -minikeys -seed -prng -byte 16,32 -mode 1-4 -gen 1-4 -s 0 -e FFFFFFFF -c c

[!] ======================================================================
[!] MAIN MODE: -brain
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Purpose:
[!] Brainwallet mode (string -> hash -> key flow).

[!] Enable:
[!] -brain                         default sha256.

[!] Submodes:
[!] -brain 1                       sha3-256.
[!] -brain 2                       keccak256.
[!] -brain 3                       blake2b-256.
[!] -brain 4                       passthrough.
[!]
[!] Named profiles:
[!] -brain-profile NAME            Owns hash mode, iteration count and
[!]                                binary/hex chaining for this run.
[!]   sha256                       Ordinary SHA-256 (legacy default).
[!]   brainflayer-sha256           Historical brainflayer SHA-256 alias.
[!]   brainwallet.org              Historical SHA-256 alias.
[!]   bitaddress / bitcoinjs       Historical SHA-256 aliases.
[!]   sha256d / sha256-hex         Two binary or lowercase-hex rounds.
[!]   sha3-256[d]                  SHA3-256, one or two binary rounds.
[!]   keccak256[d]                 Keccak-256, one or two binary rounds.
[!]   blake2b-256[d]               BLAKE2b-256, one or two binary rounds.
[!]   raw                          Right-aligned 32-byte private material.
[!]
[!] Streaming rules / combinator:
[!] -brain-rules FILE              Hashcat-compatible core rules, one per line.
[!]                                Supported: : l u c C t r d pN f q { } [ ]
[!]                                k K $X ^X TN DN 'N xNM sXY @X iNX oNX zN ZN.
[!]                                Use \xNN for a binary/literal argument.
[!] -brain-combine FILE            Stream left candidates with a right dictionary.
[!] -brain-combine-mode lr|rl|both Concatenation order, default lr.
[!] -space                         Insert one ASCII space between both words.
[!] Rules are compiled once, duplicate rules are removed, and expansions feed
[!] the existing double-buffered Metal worker without materializing the
[!] logical cross-product. Right files up to 64 MiB are resident; larger files
[!] are replayed as a bounded stream. Completed expanded candidates, not base
[!] lines, are credited by the common SpeedThreadFunc.

[!] Input / transform:
[!] -i FILE                        Brainwallet text input file. STDIN is used when -i is not set.
[!] -hex                           Input lines are hex-encoded bytes instead of text.
[!] -iter LIST                     Hash rounds list for selected -brain submode.
[!] -utf8                          UTF-8 text flow between iterations.
[!] -round N                       Plus/minus rounds around each generated key.
[!]
[!] Sequential mode:
[!] -start HEX                     First byte/payload point for seq branch.
[!] -end HEX                       Last byte/payload point for seq branch.
[!] -step HEX                      Step between seq points, default 1.
[!] -back                          Walk backward from -start.
[!] -both                          Without -end: walk both directions around -start.
[!]                                With -start/-end: + starts at -start, - starts at -end.
[!] -random                        With -start/-end, choose random points inside that range.
[!] -n N                           Seq-random span/check window.
[!]
[!] PRNG mode:
[!] -prng                          Use internal 32-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -prng64                        Use internal 64-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -gen LIST                      Generator IDs list/range.
[!] -mode LIST                     Byte extraction mode IDs list/range.
[!] -byte LIST                     Generated byte sizes list/range.
[!] -shift LIST                    Skip counts list/range.
[!] -s HEX                         PRNG start seed.
[!] -e HEX                         PRNG end seed.
[!] -random                        Randomize PRNG seed selection.
[!]
[!] Hexset sequential mode:
[!] -hexset HEXDIGITS              Hex alphabet, 1..16 unique nibbles in user order.
[!] -start HEX                     Required even-length hex lower bound.
[!] -end HEX                       Optional even-length hex upper bound.
[!]
[!] Hexset recovery mode:
[!] -recovery TEMPLATE             Inline hex template; * means one unknown hex nibble.
[!] -recovery -i FILE              Template file, one template per line.
[!] -hexset HEXDIGITS              Alphabet used to fill * positions.
[!]
[!] Example:
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -brain 2 -iter 1,2,3 -i brain.txt -c cuspex -bf bloom.blf
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -brain -brain-profile sha256d \
[!]   -brain-rules best64.rule -i phrases.txt -c c -hash HASH160
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -brain -brain-profile sha256 \
[!]   -i left.txt -brain-combine right.txt -brain-combine-mode both -space \
[!]   -c c -bf targets.blf

[!] ======================================================================
[!] MAIN MODE: -old  (Old Electrum mnemonic)
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Purpose:
[!] Electrum v1 family mode.

[!] Enable:
[!] -old

[!] Old sub-branches:
[!] A) OLD mnemonic branch: (old mnemonic)
[!]    -old
[!]    -valid                        Save valid and invalid into Valid.txt / NotValid.txt

[!] B) OLD seed-bytes branch: (old mnemonic seeds)
[!]    -old -seed
[!]    or
[!]    -old -entropy

[!] Flags for -old:
[!] File input / mnemonic branch:
[!] -i FILE                        Old Electrum mnemonic input file. STDIN is used when -i is not set.
[!] -valid                         Save valid and invalid mnemonics into Valid.txt / NotValid.txt.
[!] -deep N                        Per-chain child depth, default 20.
[!] -round N                       Plus/minus rounds around each generated key.
[!]
[!] PRNG mode:
[!] -prng                          Use internal 32-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -prng64                        Use internal 64-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -gen LIST                      Generator IDs list/range.
[!] -mode LIST                     Byte extraction mode IDs list/range.
[!] -byte LIST                     Generated byte sizes list/range.
[!] -shift LIST                    Skip counts list/range.
[!] -s HEX                         PRNG start seed.
[!] -e HEX                         PRNG end seed.
[!] -random                        Randomize PRNG seed selection.
[!]
[!] Hexset sequential mode:
[!] -hexset HEXDIGITS              Hex alphabet, 1..16 unique nibbles in user order.
[!] -start HEX                     Required even-length hex lower bound.
[!] -end HEX                       Optional even-length hex upper bound.
[!]
[!] Hexset recovery mode:
[!] -recovery TEMPLATE             Inline hex template; * means one unknown hex nibble.
[!] -recovery -i FILE              Template file, one template per line.
[!] -hexset HEXDIGITS              Alphabet used to fill * positions.
[!]
[!] Example:
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -old -valid -i old_mnemonics.txt -c cuspex

[!] ======================================================================
[!] MAIN MODE: -armory  (EASY16)
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Purpose:
[!] Treat input as Armory Easy16 paper backup.

[!] Enable:
[!] -armory

[!] Flags for -armory:
[!] File input:
[!] -i FILE                        Armory Easy16 input file. STDIN is used when -i is not set.
[!] -deep N                        Child depth.
[!] -round N                       Plus/minus rounds around each generated key.
[!]
[!] PRNG mode:
[!] -prng                          Use internal 32-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -prng64                        Use internal 64-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -gen LIST                      Generator IDs list/range.
[!] -mode LIST                     Byte extraction mode IDs list/range.
[!] -byte LIST                     Generated byte sizes list/range.
[!] -shift LIST                    Skip counts list/range.
[!] -s HEX                         PRNG start seed.
[!] -e HEX                         PRNG end seed.
[!] -random                        Randomize PRNG seed selection.
[!]
[!] Hexset recovery mode:
[!] -recovery TEMPLATE             Inline hex template; * means one unknown hex nibble.
[!] -recovery -i FILE              Template file, one template per line.
[!] -hexset HEXDIGITS              Alphabet used to fill * positions.
[!]
[!] Input note:
[!] Easy16 blocks can be split with '%' or passed in one line.

[!] NOTE:
[!] No derivation file is required for -armory Easy16.

[!] Example:
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -armory -i armory_easy16.txt -deep 30 -c cuspex

[!] ======================================================================
[!] MAIN MODE: -root  (ARMORY ROOT KEY MODE)
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Purpose:
[!] Treat input as Armory root key:
[!] 32-byte root OR 64-byte root+chaincode (usually in HEX).

[!] Enable:
[!] -root

[!] Submodes:
[!] -root 0                         default root mode.
[!] -root 1                         sha256.
[!] -root 2                         sha512.
[!] -root 3                         keccak256.
[!] -root 4                         sha3-256.
[!] -root 5                         md5.
[!] -root 6                         blake2b-256.
[!] -root 7                         passthrough.

[!] Flags for -root:
[!] File input / transform:
[!] -i FILE                        Armory root input file. STDIN is used when -i is not set.
[!] -hex                           Input lines are hex-encoded root bytes.
[!] -iter LIST                     Hash rounds list for selected -root submode.
[!] -utf8                          UTF-8 text flow between iterations.
[!] -text                          Store hash output as text payload.
[!] -deep N                        Child depth.
[!] -round N                       Plus/minus rounds around each generated key.
[!]
[!] PRNG mode:
[!] -prng                          Use internal 32-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -prng64                        Use internal 64-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -gen LIST                      Generator IDs list/range.
[!] -mode LIST                     Byte extraction mode IDs list/range.
[!] -byte LIST                     Generated byte sizes list/range.
[!] -shift LIST                    Skip counts list/range.
[!] -s HEX                         PRNG start seed.
[!] -e HEX                         PRNG end seed.
[!] -random                        Randomize PRNG seed selection.
[!]
[!] Hexset recovery mode:
[!] -recovery TEMPLATE             Inline hex template; * means one unknown hex nibble.
[!] -recovery -i FILE              Template file, one template per line.
[!] -hexset HEXDIGITS              Alphabet used to fill * positions.
[!]
[!] NOTE:
[!] -root is a separate main mode from -armory Easy16 flow.

[!] Example:
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -root 3 -iter 1,2,4 -hex -i armory_root_hex.txt -deep 30 -c cuspex

[!] ======================================================================
[!] MAIN MODE: -profanity  (Old Profanity-compatible search)
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Purpose:
[!] Reproduce vulnerable old Profanity generation on GPU.
[!] Each seed32 initializes MT19937-64, takes 4 consecutive uint64 draws,
[!] builds the base private key in Profanity word order, then walks secp256k1
[!] points forward with +G.
[!] Exact private formula:
[!] base_private(seed32) + foundId*2^192 + round.

[!] Enable:
[!] -profanity

[!] Supported targets:
[!] -c c                            BTC compressed hash160.
[!] -c u                            BTC uncompressed hash160.
[!] -c s                            BTC segwit base58 hash160.
[!] -c p                            BTC segwit p2wsh hash160.
[!] -c r                            BTC taproot hash.
[!] -c x                            secp256k1 public X coordinate.
[!] -c e                            Ethereum address.
[!] -c cu / cusr / cusrpex           Dedicated combined kernels.

[!] Flags for -profanity:
[!] -s HEX32                        Start seed32, default 00000000.
[!] -e HEX32                        End seed32, default ffffffff.
[!] -n NUMBER                       Rounds/checks per Metal lane, default 2^32.
[!] -offset HEX                     First checked round per lane, default 1.
[!]                                 Use -offset 0 only for basepoint/debug checks.
[!] -random                         Pick a random seed32 from -s..-e after each seed pass.
[!]                                 The range defaults to 00000000..ffffffff.
[!]                                 Selection is with replacement; duplicate seeds are possible.
[!] -random-seeds N                 With -random, check N sequential seed32 values after
[!]                                 each random pick, then pick a new random start.
[!]                                 Default 1 preserves old -random behavior.
[!] -hash HEX                       Prefix/target filter, target-type dependent.
[!] -target HEX                     Alias for -hash in this mode.
[!] -bf PATH                        Bloom filter(s).
[!] -xu PATH                        XOR uncompressed filter(s).
[!] -xc PATH                        XOR compressed filter(s).
[!] -xuc PATH                       XOR ultra-compressed filter(s).
[!] -xh PATH                        XOR HC filter(s).
[!] -save                           Save found keys through Profanity save path.
[!] -o FILE                         Output file, default result.txt.
[!] -device LIST                    Multi-GPU device list.
[!] -gpu-split round|seed|foundid   Multi-GPU partition mode. Default: round.
[!]                                 round: same seed/foundId domain, GPUs split ROUND windows.
[!]                                 seed: GPUs take different seed32 values from -s..-e.
[!]                                 foundid: same seed/ROUND window, GPUs split foundId ranges.
[!] -b N / -t N                     -b is physical Metal threadgroups per launch.
[!]                                 -t is forced to 256 for this mode.
[!]                                 Default grid is 16384x256 with historical foundId domain.
[!]                                 Manual -b changes active foundId count to -b*256.
[!]                                 Speed is printed only by the standard speedThread.
[!] -fsize N                        Max Profanity found records per GPU launch, default 150000.
[!] -bit N                          Manual secp precompute bits; default auto is 16 for Profanity.

[!] Notes:
[!] Profanity uses its own seed32/foundId/ROUND domain.
[!] -n always means ROUND checks per Metal lane; multiGPU coverage depends on -gpu-split.
[!] Speed is printed as point/hash target checks, not input lines.
[!] Separate target-specific kernels are kept for c/u/s/p/r/x/e/cu/cusr/cusrpex.
[!] Save format:
[!] SEED 00000000:OFFSET 0000000000000000:ROUND 0000000000000001:PRIV:<priv64>:<TYPE>:<payload>
[!] Direct search TYPE follows -c and filters: COMPRESSED/UNCOMPRESSED/SEGWIT/P2WSH/TAPROOT/XPOINT/ETH.
[!] With -save, payload formatting follows the standard key save path for that TYPE.
[!] OFFSET is foundId/lane_id. ROUND is the low addition counter.

[!] Examples:
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -profanity -s 0 -e ffff -n 4294967296 -c c -xc targets.xor
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -profanity -s 0 -e 0 -n 1024 -offset 1 -c x -hash 70519f67 -save
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -profanity -random -s 0 -e ffffffff -n 1048576 -c cusrpex -xc targets.xor
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -device 0-3 -profanity -s 0 -e ffffffff -n 4294967296 -c cusrpex -xc targets.xor

[!] ======================================================================
[!] MAIN MODE: -profanity -recovery  (Profanity public key recovery)
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Purpose:
[!] Recover a Profanity private key from a known secp256k1 public key.
[!] The GPU reverse-walks Q-kG, checks Profanity basepoint-X XOR filters,
[!] then seed-resolve/full public-key verification rejects false positives.

[!] Enable:
[!] -profanity -recovery

[!] Required input:
[!] -target HEX                     Single 33-byte compressed or 65-byte uncompressed public key.
[!] -hash HEX                       Alias for -target in this mode.
[!] -i FILE                         Batch/restart file with pubkeys and per-key round offsets.
[!] -xc PATH                        GPU compressed XOR basepoint filter.
[!] -xu PATH                        GPU uncompressed XOR basepoint filter.
[!] -xuc PATH                       GPU ultra-compressed XOR basepoint filter.
[!] -xh PATH                        GPU HC XOR basepoint filter.
[!]                                 At least one GPU XOR basepoint filter is required.

[!] Optional verification:
[!] -xx PATH                        Optional CPU XOR uncompressed check for GPU hits.
[!]                                 Without -xx, GPU hits go directly to seed-resolve.
[!]                                 Use together with a GPU XOR filter.

[!] Flags for -profanity -recovery:
[!] -s HEX32                        Seed-resolve start seed32, default 00000000.
[!] -e HEX32                        Seed-resolve end seed32, default ffffffff.
[!] -offset HEX                     Single-target reverse-walk round restart offset, default 0.
[!] -n NUMBER                       Only with -i FILE: rounds per pubkey pass, default 16384.
[!] -device LIST                    Multi-GPU device list.
[!] -b N / -t N                     Optional manual launch geometry.
[!] -bit N                          Manual secp precompute bits; default auto is 16 for Profanity.

[!] Batch/restart file format for -i FILE:
[!] <pubkey>
[!] <pubkey>:<offset_hex>
[!] <pubkey>:<offset_hex>:found
[!] Pubkey accepts 02/03 compressed or 04 uncompressed hex, optional 0x prefix.
[!] Offset is the reverse-walk ROUND offset, rewritten as 16 lowercase hex.
[!] :found entries are skipped. Comments and blank lines are preserved.
[!] After a completed window, offset advances by exactly -n, not by GPU count.
[!] With one active pubkey, a verified found marks :found and exits.
[!] With multiple active pubkeys, found entries are skipped and remaining keys cycle.

[!] Filter format:
[!] Profanity basepoint filter source stores one 20-byte item per seed/lane basepoint.
[!] Current production format uses the first 20 bytes of canonical affine X.
[!] GPU filters supported: -xu, -xc, -xuc, -xh.
[!] Hyper filters are allowed, but noisy hits still must pass seed-resolve/full pubkey verification.
[!] Large -xu may be impractical on 24GB GPUs; it remains supported like other modes.

[!] Notes:
[!] Single-target -target/-hash recovery continues in host-polled GPU batches
[!] until stopped or a verified key is found.
[!] File mode -i FILE uses -n as fixed per-pubkey windows.
[!] Address/hash160-only targets are invalid here: recovery needs the public point Q.
[!] Save format is the same Profanity line format described in -profanity.

[!] Examples:
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -profanity -recovery -target 02... -xc PROFANITY_PUBS.xor_c -xx PROFANITY_PUBS.xor_u -save
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -device 0-3 -profanity -recovery -hash 04... -offset 1 -xuc PROFANITY_PUBS.xor_uc -save
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -profanity -recovery -target 04... -s 0 -e ffffffff -xh PROFANITY_PUBS.xor_hc
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -profanity -recovery -i pubs.txt -n 16384 -xc PROFANITY_PUBS.xor_c -save

[!] ======================================================================
[!] MAIN MODE: -recovery  (Mnemonic recovery mode)
[!] ======================================================================
[!] Purpose:
[!]   Mnemonic recovery mode from template phrase or template file.
[!]   Requires derivations file: -d FILE
[!]
[!] Input forms:
[!]   -recovery "template phrase with * placeholders"
[!]   -recovery -i FILE
[!] Recovery options:
[!]   -wordlist FILE
[!]   -pbkdf N
[!]   -electrum [seg], -128, -ton / -TON (optional behavior toggles)
[!]
[!] Examples:
[!]   ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -recovery "legal winner thank year wave sausage worth useful legal winner thank *" -d derivations.txt
[!]   ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -recovery -i templates.txt -wordlist wordlists/bip39-en.txt -d derivations.txt
[!]


[!] ======================================================================
[!] EXTRA MODIFIERS USED MOSTLY WITH MNEMONIC/ENTROPY FLOWS
[!] ======================================================================
[!] -electrum [seg]                 Electrum v2 style mode (optional seg variant).
[!] -128                            Electrum 128 style.
[!] -ton / -TON                     TON mnemonic style toggle.

[!] ======================================================================
[!] PRNG CONTROL (FOR PRNG-CAPABLE MODES)
[!] ======================================================================
[!] -prng                           Use internal 32-bit PRNG backend.
[!] -prng64                         Use internal 64-bit PRNG backend.

[!] -gen LIST                       Generator IDs list/range.
[!] -mode LIST                      Byte extraction mode IDs list/range.
[!] -byte LIST                      Generated byte sizes list/range.
[!] -shift LIST                     Skip counts list/range.
[!] -s HEX                          Start seed (HEX).
[!] -e HEX                          End seed (HEX).
[!] -random                         Randomize start seed.

[!] Defaults:
[!] 32-bit backend: -s 00000000, -e FFFFFFFF.
[!] 64-bit backend: -s 0000000000000000, -e FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF.
[!] Supported catalog ranges:
[!] 32-bit backend: -gen 1-489, -mode 1-762.
[!] 64-bit backend: -gen 1-223, -mode 1-218.
[!] if -gen not set: all supported gens.
[!] if -mode not set: all supported modes.
[!] if -shift not set: 0.

[!] Full references:
[!] -prng_help                      Print all 32-bit generators/modes and exit.
[!] -prng64_help                    Print all 64-bit generators/modes and exit.

[!] ======================================================================
[!] COMMON CHECKLIST BEFORE RUN
[!] ======================================================================
[!] 1) Use the current mode help above to see whether -d FILE is required.
[!] 2) For seq-random, set both -start and -end.
[!] 3) -back and -both are mutually exclusive; last flag wins.
[!] 4) Verify filter/input paths are readable.

[!] ======================================================================
[!] EXAMPLES
[!] ======================================================================
[!] [!] DEFAULT MNEMONIC FROM FILE [!]
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -i input.txt -d derivations.txt -c cuspex -bf bloom.blf

[!] [!] MNEMONIC + ELECTRUM + PASSPHRASE FILE [!]
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -mnemonic -pass pass.txt -electrum -d derivations.txt -i input.txt -c cuspex

[!] [!] ENTROPY SHA256 CUSTOM SIZES [!]
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -entropy 1 -sizes 16,24,32 -d derivations.txt -i entropy.txt -c cuspex

[!] [!] BIP32 MODE [!]
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -bip32 0 -hex -d derivations.txt -i passphrases.txt -c cuspex

[!] [!] SEED MODE [!]
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -seed -hex -d derivations.txt -i seeds_hex.txt -c cuspex

[!] [!] HMAC MODE [!]
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -hmac -hex -d derivations.txt -i hmac_hex.txt -c cuspex

[!] [!] PRIV MODE (256 rotate-left keys from 1 key) [!]
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -priv 0  -hex -i keys_hex.txt -c cuspex -bf bloom.blf

[!] [!] OLD ELECTRUM VALID SPLIT [!]
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -old -valid -i old_mnemonics.txt -c cuspex

[!] [!] ARMORY EASY16 [!]
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -armory -i armory_easy16.txt -deep 30 -c cuspex

[!] [!] ARMORY ROOT [!]
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -root 3 -iter 1,2,4 -hex -i armory_root_hex.txt -deep 30 -c cuspex

[!] [!] PROFANITY SEARCH [!]
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -profanity -s 0 -e ffff -n 4294967296 -c c -xc targets.xor

[!] [!] PROFANITY RECOVERY [!]
[!] ./METAL_CRYPTO_TOOLKIT -profanity -recovery -target 02... -xc PROFANITY_PUBS.xor_c -xx PROFANITY_PUBS.xor_u -save
)HELP";

static bool isHelpArg(const char* arg) {
    return arg != nullptr && (std::strcmp(arg, "-h") == 0 || std::strcmp(arg, "-help") == 0);
}

static bool has_help_arg(int argc, char** argv) {
    for (int i = 1; i < argc; ++i) {
        if (isHelpArg(argv[i])) return true;
    }
    return false;
}

static bool has_arg(int argc, char** argv, const char* needle) {
    for (int i = 1; i < argc; ++i) {
        if (std::strcmp(argv[i], needle) == 0) return true;
    }
    return false;
}

static bool is_help_topic_arg(const char* arg, const char* dashed) {
    if (arg == nullptr || dashed == nullptr) {
        return false;
    }
    if (std::strcmp(arg, dashed) == 0) {
        return true;
    }
    return dashed[0] == '-' && std::strcmp(arg, dashed + 1) == 0;
}

static HelpTopic detect_help_topic(int argc, char** argv) {
    for (int i = 1; i < argc; ++i) {
        const char* arg = argv[i];
        if (arg == nullptr || isHelpArg(arg)) continue;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-der_thread")) return HelpTopic::DerThread;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-pass_thread")) return HelpTopic::PassThread;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-profanity")) {
            return has_arg(argc, argv, "-recovery") ? HelpTopic::ProfanityRecovery : HelpTopic::Profanity;
        }
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-priv")) {
            if (has_arg(argc, argv, "-hamming")) return HelpTopic::Hamming;
            return has_arg(argc, argv, "-recovery") ? HelpTopic::PrivRecovery : HelpTopic::Priv;
        }
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-hamming")) return HelpTopic::Hamming;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-warpwallet")) return HelpTopic::WarpWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-algorand")) return HelpTopic::Algorand;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-monerowallet")) return HelpTopic::MoneroWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-monero")) return HelpTopic::Monero;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-kangaroo")) return HelpTopic::Kangaroo;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-bsgs")) return HelpTopic::Bsgs;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-keyrepair")) return HelpTopic::KeyRepair;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-nonce")) return HelpTopic::Nonce;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-vanity")) return HelpTopic::Vanity;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-create2")) return HelpTopic::Create2;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-hdpath")) return HelpTopic::HdPath;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-poetry")) return HelpTopic::Poetry;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-minikeys")) {
            return has_arg(argc, argv, "-seed") ? HelpTopic::MinikeysSeed : HelpTopic::Minikeys;
        }
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-old")) {
            return (has_arg(argc, argv, "-seed") || has_arg(argc, argv, "-entropy")) ? HelpTopic::OldSeed : HelpTopic::Old;
        }
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-armory")) {
            return has_arg(argc, argv, "-root") ? HelpTopic::Root : HelpTopic::Armory;
        }
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-recovery")) {
            if (has_arg(argc, argv, "-profanity")) return HelpTopic::ProfanityRecovery;
            if (has_arg(argc, argv, "-priv")) return HelpTopic::PrivRecovery;
            return HelpTopic::Recovery;
        }
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-seed")) {
            if (has_arg(argc, argv, "-old")) return HelpTopic::OldSeed;
            if (has_arg(argc, argv, "-minikeys")) return HelpTopic::MinikeysSeed;
            return HelpTopic::Seed;
        }
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-entropy") && has_arg(argc, argv, "-old")) return HelpTopic::OldSeed;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-mnemonic")) return HelpTopic::Mnemonic;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-xp")) return HelpTopic::Xp;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-hmac")) return HelpTopic::Hmac;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-entropy")) return HelpTopic::Entropy;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-bip32")) return HelpTopic::Bip32;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-brain")) return HelpTopic::Brain;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-root")) return HelpTopic::Root;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-keystore")) return HelpTopic::Keystore;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-walletdat")) return HelpTopic::WalletDat;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-walletjs")) return HelpTopic::WalletJs;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-browservault")) return HelpTopic::BrowserVault;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-copaywallet")) return HelpTopic::CopayWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-terrawallet")) return HelpTopic::TerraWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-bitshareswallet")) return HelpTopic::BitSharesWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-yoroiwallet")) return HelpTopic::YoroiWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-substratewallet")) return HelpTopic::SubstrateWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-blockchainwallet")) return HelpTopic::BlockchainWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-multibitwallet")) return HelpTopic::MultiBitWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-bip38")) return HelpTopic::Bip38;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-ethpresale")) return HelpTopic::EthPresale;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-androidwallet")) return HelpTopic::AndroidWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-slip39")) return HelpTopic::Slip39;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-aezeed")) return HelpTopic::Aezeed;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-stronghold")) return HelpTopic::Stronghold;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-eth2validator")) return HelpTopic::Eth2Validator;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-bisqwallet")) return HelpTopic::BisqWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-dogechainwallet")) return HelpTopic::DogechainWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-stellarwallet")) return HelpTopic::StellarWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-electrumwallet")) return HelpTopic::ElectrumWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-exodusseco")) return HelpTopic::ExodusSeco;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-bitcoinjwallet")) return HelpTopic::BitcoinJWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-multidogewallet")) return HelpTopic::BitcoinJWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-armorywallet")) return HelpTopic::ArmoryWallet;
        if (is_help_topic_arg(arg, "-walletscan")) return HelpTopic::WalletScan;
    }
    return HelpTopic::Short;
}

static const char* help_topic_command(HelpTopic topic) {
    switch (topic) {
    case HelpTopic::Mnemonic: return "-mnemonic";
    case HelpTopic::Recovery: return "-recovery";
    case HelpTopic::DerThread: return "-der_thread";
    case HelpTopic::PassThread: return "-pass_thread";
    case HelpTopic::Priv: return "-priv";
    case HelpTopic::PrivRecovery: return "-priv -recovery";
    case HelpTopic::Hamming: return "-priv -hamming";
    case HelpTopic::WarpWallet: return "-warpwallet";
    case HelpTopic::Algorand: return "-algorand";
    case HelpTopic::Monero: return "-monero";
    case HelpTopic::MoneroWallet: return "-monerowallet";
    case HelpTopic::Kangaroo: return "-kangaroo";
    case HelpTopic::Bsgs: return "-bsgs";
    case HelpTopic::KeyRepair: return "-keyrepair";
    case HelpTopic::Nonce: return "-nonce";
    case HelpTopic::Vanity: return "-vanity";
    case HelpTopic::Create2: return "-create2";
    case HelpTopic::HdPath: return "-hdpath";
    case HelpTopic::Poetry: return "-poetry";
    case HelpTopic::Minikeys: return "-minikeys";
    case HelpTopic::MinikeysSeed: return "-minikeys -seed";
    case HelpTopic::Xp: return "-xp";
    case HelpTopic::Seed: return "-seed";
    case HelpTopic::Hmac: return "-hmac";
    case HelpTopic::Entropy: return "-entropy";
    case HelpTopic::Bip32: return "-bip32";
    case HelpTopic::Brain: return "-brain";
    case HelpTopic::Old: return "-old";
    case HelpTopic::OldSeed: return "-old -seed";
    case HelpTopic::Armory: return "-armory";
    case HelpTopic::Root: return "-root";
    case HelpTopic::Profanity: return "-profanity";
    case HelpTopic::ProfanityRecovery: return "-profanity -recovery";
    case HelpTopic::Keystore: return "-keystore";
    case HelpTopic::WalletDat: return "-walletdat";
    case HelpTopic::WalletJs: return "-walletjs";
    case HelpTopic::BrowserVault: return "-browservault";
    case HelpTopic::CopayWallet: return "-copaywallet";
    case HelpTopic::TerraWallet: return "-terrawallet";
